{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user initiated a cobbler pipeline \"stitch\" task (#5634) for generation-run44 of the go-unix-utils project. The project reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils utilities in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The task prompt is massive, containing the full project context (VISION, ARCHITECTURE, SPECIFICATIONS, road-map, all pkg/ source code, coding standards, execution constitution). However, the task description states: \"Cobbler measure is calling Claude to propose task 0 for generation generation-run44. This issue will be closed automatically when measure completes.\" The requirement_states section shows SRDs srd004-ts, srd105-stty, srd110-pr, and srd111-ptx all have requirements in \"ready\" status, indicating these are candidates for implementation. No explicit \"Requirements\" or \"Files to Create/Modify\" sections were provided in the task, which would normally be present in a concrete stitch task.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils utilities\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against Homebrew GNU reference binary (g-prefixed: gcat, gls, etc.)\n   - pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests harness for side-by-side comparison of stdout, stderr, exit code\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() in all cmd/ utilities\n   - Cobbler pipeline: measure (task planning) → stitch (code generation)\n   - SRD-driven development: Software Requirements Documents define all requirements\n   - LC_ALL=C constraint for all differential tests\n   - Generation runs: code is deleted and regenerated from specs\n   - Git managed externally by orchestrator - never run git commands\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines hard limit\n   - File size limit: 500 lines of production code\n   - Write all source files before running build/test commands\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `.cobbler/requirements.yaml` (first 200 lines read)\n     - Shows requirement status for srd001-testutils (R1.1-R5.2, mix of complete/uncertain), srd002-sys (R1.1-R3.3, all complete), srd003-format (R1.1-R2.7+, complete)\n     - Important for understanding what requirements still need implementation\n   - All pkg/ source code was provided inline in the prompt:\n     - `pkg/encutil/decode.go` and `pkg/encutil/encode.go` - encoding/decoding utilities\n     - `pkg/format/` - color.go, humansize.go, pad.go, align.go, columns.go\n     - `pkg/hashutil/hashconfig.go` and `pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go` - hash formatting and verification\n     - `pkg/sizeparse/parse.go` - human-readable size string parsing\n     - `pkg/sys/` - fileinfo.go, signal.go, sigpipe.go, stat_darwin.go, terminal.go\n     - `pkg/testutils/` - build.go, difftest.go\n   - Package contracts defined for: srd001-testutils, srd002-sys, srd003-format, srd086-hashutil, srd087-sizeparse, srd088-encutil\n   - Requirement states showing \"ready\" requirements for: srd004-ts (R1.1-R10.3), srd105-stty (R1.1-R7.3), srd110-pr (R1.1-R5.2), srd111-ptx (R1.1-R5.2)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only one tool call was made before the summary request.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - I began by reading `.cobbler/requirements.yaml` to understand which requirements need implementation. Only 200 lines were read (covering srd001-testutils, srd002-sys, and beginning of srd003-format statuses). I had not yet reached the requirements for the SRDs shown in requirement_states (srd004-ts, srd105-stty, srd110-pr, srd111-ptx).\n   - No implementation work has been started.\n\n6. All user messages:\n